nt><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAO CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORII, MASAYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORII MASAYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORII, MASAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a polyurethane foam which comprises reacting a polyol ingredient with an isocyanate ingredient in the presence of a catalyst comprising a compound represented by formula (I), (wherein p is an integer of 4 to 8) and a compound having a primary amino group and a tertiary amino group in the molecule, a foaming agent, and a foam stabilizer. The polyurethane foam obtained by the process is suitable for use as a building material, a heat insulation material for electrical refrigerators, cold storages, bathtubs, etc., a material for interior automotive trims, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce procédé de production de mousse de polyuréthane consiste à faire réagir un polyol avec un isocyanate en présence d'un catalyseur renfermant un composé représenté par la formule (I), formule dans laquelle p représente un nombre entier d'une valeur comprise entre 4 et 8, et un composé possédant un groupe amino primaire ainsi qu'un groupe amino tertiaire dans la molécule, un agent moussant et un stabilisateur de mousse. La mousse de polyuréthane obtenue par ce procédé peut être avantageusement utilisée comme matériau de construction, d'isolation thermique pour des réfrigérateurs électriques, pour des stockages froids, des baignoires, etc., comme matériau pour des ornementations intérieures d'automobile, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>